bool g_adminDestroy = false, g_tearingDown = false;   // our own destroys (retire / supersede / teardown) are not "gone"
// P6j (verify-p6c HIGH-1) - THE ENGINE'S OWN TEARDOWN, AS A SPAN OF ITS OWN, AND NOTHING ELSE.
// g_tearingDown means "our destroys are the engine's, not removals": it is raised at a teardown and its ONLY clear
// anywhere in the tree is the first SquadContainer::loadFromDisk of the next world. That is the correct span for
// classifying destroys and the wrong one for refusing to invent. The teardown that fires on a world LOAD is
// resetGame, so P6c's invent gate - which read g_tearingDown - was up from the start of the load until the engine
// first touched a squad container, i.e. across the opening stretch of every world load, and a refusal on the
// bar-fly path DESTROYS that town's resident list for the whole life of the world (the list is filled once per
// Town object). The hazard the gate exists for is much shorter: g_loadedHere has no clock and keeps answering 1 for
// the world being freed, and it is wiped by ZonesForgetHeldGrid inside TeardownBroadcastLateFlags - 171 ms after the
// raise in T228 (78.079 -> 78.250).
