// every reader of the four grids and the two clocks now sees a kept map across a teardown while the relay is up.
// The two that change behaviour are the sleep hook (HeldByOtherTS answers 1 or 0 from the last map instead of -1,
// which is what E33 keeps the grid across orig_* FOR, extended by the width of this function) and the announce
// pass's freshness guard in worldsync (RelayMapFresh() answers true, so a pass judges from a map at most a second
